      "explanation": "The human corpus luteum starts regressing ~10 days after ovulation.\n\nOvulation occurs on day 14, and the day corpus luteum begins to regress on day 25 of the menstrual cycle.\n\nTherefore,\nDays after ovulation when corpus luteum starts regressing = 25 - 14 = 11 days.\n\nThe human corpus luteum is programmed to live for 14 days, plus or minus 2 days (corpus luteum of menstruation)."
    },
